Can models that choose from supplied actions guide an agent all the way to a goal? System-One Control Bench tests this across 100 symbolic gridworld puzzles, ten input conditions and five action spaces. An exact solver identifies every optimal move, including ties. With full context, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (reasoning) has the highest success rate among the models, 80%; Jev completes 57% of games. Adding simulated action outcomes to the map improves Jev's success rate by 16 percentage points. Longer sequences of actions do not consistently help. With full context, Jev is 90% optimal on an exam of 495 scripted positions shared by all models and 79% optimal in its own games after equal puzzle weighting, with 57% game success. Strong performance on scripted positions does not establish reliable navigation.
